{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103732","id":2377415312,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6NtHqQ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103732","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103732.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103732.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103732","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103732/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103732/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103732/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/2997fc59b5945da9f4a0af182e589efd256aef48","number":103732,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Proof of concept proposal for Variant string-formatting.","user":{"login":"mpsalisbury","id":91654,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNjU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91654?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury","html_url":"https://github.com/mpsalisbury","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"With an eye towards adding slot formatting to the [f-string implementation](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103239), this PR implements a formatting configuration language similar to the [Python format specification mini-language](https://docs.python.org/3/library/string.html#formatspec). The core implementation is a new class FormatSpec that contains the formatting configuration, can parse a text description of that configuration, and can format a Variant using that configuration. I've also embedded this formatting into String::format so that you can specify a format spec in a format template (e.g. `\"foo {0:#_x}\".format([1234560])` -> `\"foo 0x12_d680\"`). And as mentioned above, if this is accepted I'd expect to integrate this into the f-string implementation to support embedded format strings (e.g. `f\"foo {1234560:#_x}\"`).\r\n\r\nThere is significant usage documentation attached to the [FormatSpec struct](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/compare/master...mpsalisbury:godot:string-format#diff-ecfadcb1f8fb1247111f44d736274558654e23a28afeecd131a9efddef8da1d9R760) (mirroring the Python spec), and many usage examples in [test_string.h](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/compare/master...mpsalisbury:godot:string-format#diff-d1036e3c844034f9afa5867e9266efe525bcd16c773be6b70a1d8deb83005bc0R2322).\r\n\r\n## Some implementation notes\r\n\r\n* This implementation leans towards the existing Godot string formatting patterns, such as supporting vector printing, rather than strictly following the Python patterns.\r\n* I did not implement scientific or general floating point formatting. It would be easy to integrate those once we have precision-honoring implementations in String (for instance, while there is a String::num_scientific() method now, it currently calls sprintf with the 'g' format (not 'e'), and it doesn't accept a precision/decimals argument). \r\n* My integration with String::format leaves the existing support for placeholder templates alone and will only activate when the default placeholder `'{_}'` is used. This means that position-based placeholders (e.g. `{}`) and alternate keys (e.g. `$_`) will continue to work, just without the new formatting capabilities.\r\n\r\n## Open Issues\r\n\r\n* I have not yet looked into performance\r\n* I have not yet looked into syntax highlighting\r\n* I noticed that the existing vector formatting implementation considers that some platforms implement real_t as a float and some as a double. My platform (mac) uses a float, so I don't know how the implementation will work on a real_t==double platform. I presume the build/integration tests will reveal this.\r\n\r\nCloses https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/2004\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github